# Cross-Site Scripting

## What is Cross-site scripting (XSS)?
 This is a web application vulnerability that allows a user/an attacker to inject malicous javascript code into the website's original code,
 which is then executed on the victim's browser.

## TYPES OF XSS
 ### Reflected XSS
  -This is a type of XSS vulnerability where the malicious code is injected into a request and immediately reflected back to the user's
  browserand then executed.
  - It is not stored in the database.
  - It happens in search result, error message or any other response that includes the input that was sent to the server.

   EXAMPLE
 -Normal URL - https://shopping.com/search?q=keyboard (The result that will be shown will be the keyboards because you searched 
  for keyboards)
 -Malicious URL -https://shopping.com/search?q=<script>alert(1)</script>(The browser will execute this and a popup will appear and
  show 1.)

  
